From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Moritz=20Mei=C3=9Felbach?= <moritz@glassine.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:38:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] freedreno: chunked submits (FD_CHUNK_*), off by default

A long sysmem batch is cut into several kernel submits (chunks), so the CP
has a yield point every few GPU-ms and a high-priority ring (the e-ink panel
engine's) gets the GPU within one chunk instead of within one app frame.

- fd_ringbuffer_split() closes the current cmd of a growable ring and marks
  it as the end of a submit group; msm's submit path starts a new ioctl
  after each marked cmd.
- FD_CHUNK_US / FD_CHUNK_DRAWS / FD_CHUNK_COST: when to cut (an estimate of
  the open chunk's GPU time, a draw count, or both).
- FD_CHUNK_ADAPT (on with FD_CHUNK_US): GPU timestamps around chunks and
  whole batches scale the estimate per context, so a chunk is about
  FD_CHUNK_US of GPU time whatever the app's draws cost.
- FD_CHUNK_BUSY: a context cuts only while its own GPU work fills most of
  the wall time; a light app leaves gaps the other ring uses anyway.
- FD_CHUNK_NOMERGE=1: one ioctl per gallium batch, no merging of deferred
  submits.

Without FD_CHUNK_* nothing changes.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (unreviewed; tested only on the A509)
